bibliograph-worker (0.2.10-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.10 release: Goodreads WAF handling and the rebuilt HappyView payload.

    - Treat AWS WAF/Cloudflare challenge pages as provider failures instead of
      empty answers: detect x-amzn-waf-action, 202 responses and challenge body
      markers, fail the logical request immediately, and trip the Goodreads
      breaker (60s) on a block. Genuine 429/5xx keep retries with a 1s->8s
      jittered ladder, and redirect loops map to a 502 provider error.
    - Use coherent rotating browser header profiles, keep /search on a bare
      */* Accept (any explicit Accept self-redirects), and cache successful HTML
      for 24h in a bounded process-local LRU. resolve-format now reports a
      challenge as ProviderUnavailable rather than FormatNotFound.
    - Pairs with a rebuilt HappyView payload at the same image version
      (2.17.4-2): shelf/status writes find rows by record fields and mint TIDs,
      listFollowees uses the encoded cursor, and getShelversOfBook keys on the
      book URI (see the bibliograph-happyview package files).

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:20:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.2.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.9 release: fix the Goodreads ISBN lookup used by /resolve-format.

    - Goodreads 302s /search?q=<isbn> back to itself when asked for
      text/html,application/xhtml+xml, so the resolver answered 502
      ProviderUnavailable for every ISBN. ISBN identifiers (ISBN-10 and
      ISBN-13) now go straight to /book/isbn/<isbn13> (ISBN-10 normalised
      first), which redirects once to /book/show/<id> and parses as a book
      page.
    - If the book page is missing or yields no candidate, the provider falls
      back to /search with the default Accept header, which follows the single
      redirect instead of looping. Numeric Goodreads ids keep using byId and
      the existing 401/403 handling is unchanged.
    - Add provider tests covering the ISBN paths, search fallback, redirect
      handling and the existing book/search parsing.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:40:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.2.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.8 release: Goodreads-only edition format resolver.

    - Add POST /resolve-format to the loopback admin API (lib/resolve-format.js):
      it validates 1-10 ISBN-10/13 values, rejects empty/oversized lists and
      checksum failures, normalises to ISBN-13 and dedupes while preserving
      order.
    - Ask only the Goodreads provider (byIdentifier, sequential) and return the
      first non-empty candidate format as {isbn, format, source:"goodreads"};
      the hydration fallback chain is never consulted. No result is a 404
      FormatNotFound, a provider failure a 502 ProviderUnavailable.
    - The resolver performs no database, outbox or PDS writes; applying the
      value is the admin UI's decision.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.2.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.7 release: ISBNdb author normalization and the conflict backfill.

    - Add an ISBNdb-specific author parser (lib/isbndb-names.js) that rewrites
      unambiguous "Last, First" values to display order, handles generational
      and professional suffixes and name particles (including trailing ones),
      and derives the normalized comma form as nameInverted. Ambiguous,
      organizational, multi-author and malformed values are left untouched.
    - Use the parser in the ISBNdb provider and persist nameInverted at ingest
      without overwriting a curated value; admin candidate normalization keeps
      it through imports.
    - Ship scripts/normalize-isbndb-author-names.mjs (dry run by default) for
      pre-existing rows: --apply updates name/name_inverted only; optional
      --merge-conflicts folds an inverted duplicate into one display-order
      contributor via identifier-bag or unique display-order match, unions
      identifiers, repoints edition links with positions/roles/refs intact and
      deletes the source only after a savepoint-protected merge. Triggers queue
      republication; the script never writes pds_outbox or talks to the PDS.
    - Add the normalize:isbndb-authors package script and document the backfill.
      The production data repair already ran; the script ships for re-use.

